(
K13 follow-up (2026-10-06): an element without a yield law reports
materi_plasti_f = 0 (the Professional 02-08-2026), not the internal
"no yield law" value -1e10. Derived from the Professional test
tension_direct1 (one element with tension_direct 0 on its element_normal,
the element of nodes 1 2 elastic) with materi_strain_elasti/_plasti/materi_plasti_f
added: f 0 at every node (GNU before: -1e10 at nodes 1 2, -3.3e9 at the
shared nodes 3 4). Original test text:
 test tension limit plasticity
  The lower element has a tension limit 0.0 on the element_normal 
  The element_normal in the lower element actually is the vertical direction.
  So the verical stress sigyy should become 0.0
)

echo -no
number_of_space_dimensions 2
materi_velocity
materi_displacement
materi_strain_total
materi_strain_elasti
materi_strain_plasti
materi_plasti_f
materi_stress
end_initia

node 1  0 0
node 2  1 0
node 3  0 1
node 4  1 1
node 5  0 2
node 6  1 2
element 1  -quad4 1 2 3 4
element 2  -quad4 3 4 5 6

element_group 1 1
element_group 2 2

group_type 1  -materi
group_materi_elasti_young 1  1.0

group_type 2  -materi
group_materi_elasti_young 2  1.0
group_materi_plasti_tension_direct 2  0.0
group_materi_plasti_tension_direct_normal_automatic 2  -yes

bounda_dof  0  -ra 1 2 -ra -velx -vely
bounda_dof  1  -ra 5 6 -ra -vely
bounda_time 1  1.

control_timestep 0  1. 1.
(
control_print    0  -time_current -node_dof
)

target_item    0  -node_dof 1 -sigyy
target_value   0  0. 1.e-8
target_item    1  -node_dof 1 -f
target_value   1  0. 1.e-12
target_item    2  -node_dof 3 -f
target_value   2  0. 1.e-12
end_data
